  "worked_solution": "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $M$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
